final bullet: 'Output labels-<content_hash>.jsonl + Markdown report'","norm_id":"n109c11ea08f4d598","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executing agent must invent the JSONL row structure; a downstream consumer of labels-<hash>.jsonl cannot rely on stable field names."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["vague/subjective terms present: better"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State the single source of the 'closed' predicate in clean_close (e.g. reuse the same 'most-recent STATUS with status==closed' the git-walk already computes for latest_close_ts) so the boolean and its timestamp are derived consistently.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.435,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The plan defines clean_close as 'closed AND NOT escape_signals AND (now - latest_close_ts).days >= CLEAN_CLOSE_MIN_DAYS' but never says whether 'closed' is show_ticket()'s compiled status or 'the MOST RECENT STATUS event with data[\"status\"]==\"closed\"' from the git-walk.","The plan pairs 'closed' with latest_close_ts, which it DOES source from 'the MOST RECENT STATUS event with data[\"status\"] == \"closed\"' — leaving it ambiguous whether the boolean and the timestamp share that source or diverge to show_ticket's status.","A divergence is observable: a ticket reopened after its last close STATUS (current status 'open' in show_ticket) still has a most-recent close STATUS, so a STATUS-walk-derived 'closed' would be True while show_ticket status would be 'open' (the reopened escape signal already handles this, but the two readers can disagree)."],"finding":"clean_close's 'closed' predicate has no specified source, despite the plan using two independent ticket-level readers (show_ticket for close_class/inbound_deps, and a reimplemented STATUS-event git-walk for reopen/force_close and for latest_close_ts).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa560b1feb063f3b0","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Ticket-level labels' (clean_close = closed AND NOT escape_signals AND ...)","norm_id":"n1c2d08580cede4f7","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reopened-then-left-open ticket: STATUS-walk sees a latest close STATUS; show_ticket status is 'open' — the two sources disagree on 'closed'.","An administratively force-closed ticket whose latest STATUS is 'closed' but which the git-walk force_close signal already flags."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Define clean_close's 'closed' as: a most-recent STATUS event with data[\"status\"]==\"closed\" exists (the same event that supplies latest_close_ts) — deriving both from the STATUS-event walk in one pass, rather than mixing show_ticket status with the git-walk timestamp.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a parity guard (a shared fixture or a test asserting labels.py's reopen_count/force_close/completion_verifier_fail_count match the miner's on the same event dict) to prevent silent drift.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'reopen_count/force_close/completion_verifier_fail_count REIMPLEMENTED in labels.py (mirroring the miner)'","Context notes mine_outcome_corpus.py is 'docs-tree, not importable from src/', justifying reimplementation but leaving two copies of the same logic."],"finding":"reopen_count, force_close, and completion_verifier_fail_count are REIMPLEMENTED in labels.py 'mirroring the miner' (mine_outcome_corpus.py, docs-tree, not importable), but the plan provides no guard against the two implementations drifting.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0c01e4d50ae8211c","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach, 'Ticket-level event source' bullet","norm_id":"na067ceba625d4067","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The miner's definition of a reopen or force_close changes; labels.py silently computes a different value, and no test catches the divergence."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a unit test that runs both the miner functions and the labels.py reimplementations over an identical per-ticket event dict and asserts equality.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the concurrency/reentrancy contract for the REBAR_TRACKER_DIR mutation (single-process/serial only, or pass tracker_git_root through show_ticket instead of mutating a global) and confirm the finally restores the original pre-loop value.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan quote: \"per store_name, tracker_git_root in store_roots, temporarily set os.environ['REBAR_TRACKER_DIR'] = tracker_git_root (restored finally) around show_ticket(ticket_id, include_inbound=True)\"","Plan states config.tracker_dir_override() reads REBAR_TRACKER_DIR 'winning verbatim over any config' — a global, shared consumer of the mutated key.","os.environ is process-global; a set/restore window per loop iteration is not atomic and not safe if the derivation runs concurrently or if show_ticket triggers concurrent config reads."],"finding":"The plan mutates process-global state os.environ['REBAR_TRACKER_DIR'] inside the per-store loop to redirect show_ticket, but does not address reentrancy/concurrency: config.tracker_dir_override() reads this key verbatim, so if labels.py is invoked concurrently in one process (or show_ticket spawns anything reading config mid-window), the set-then-restore window is a check-then-act race that can point show_ticket at the wrong tracker root.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7ae9ed57b9451ff2","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Ticket-level event source (multi-store, env override)': \"temporarily set os.environ['REBAR_TRACKER_DIR'] = tracker_git_root (restored finally) around show_ticket(...)\"","norm_id":"n5dc574f5c3643ce2","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two labels.py derivations (or one with any concurrent config-reading work) overlap: iteration for store A sets REBAR_TRACKER_DIR to A while store B's show_ticket reads it, yielding ticket data from the wrong store and mislabeled escape signals.","A finally-restore that restores to a prior loop iteration's value (rather than the original pre-loop value) leaves REBAR_TRACKER_DIR dangling if the caller relied on the original process env."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Prefer threading the tracker root explicitly into show_ticket (or a context-scoped override) rather than mutating os.environ; if the env approach stays, document that the tool must run serially in-process and restore the captured original value, not the previous iteration's.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that _enumerate_event_blobs is enumerated once per store and the uuid->blob match is done against that single enumeration (not re-enumerated per cache row).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5a","E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.501,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'_enumerate_event_blobs applies NO content-type filter — it returns EVERY event blob'","'per cache row's review_event_uuid, re-read that SAME REVIEW_RESULT blob's data via corpus._enumerate_event_b